# Test-project outputs

The ladder programs live in `src/test/resources/test-projects/0N-name/`
(`project.kira`, `src/`, `expected.txt`). `TestProjectsRunTest`, part of
`./gradlew test`, compiles each with the CLI to C and JS, runs the C binary and
the JS on node, and diffs stdout with `expected.txt`; 01-hello and 04-classes
also run on Python, 01-hello and 09-stdlib also through g++. It also checks the
C and the JS runtime preludes are byte-identical across the projects. A
missing toolchain skips that leg's run, never its compile.

`TyperDeclTest` dumps the same projects' symbols against
`src/test/resources/typer/decls/test-projects/*.txt`.

## Minification

Generated user layers are **minified + obfuscated by default** (`OutputMinifier`):
comments/whitespace stripped, user identifiers renamed, `main` + extern/opaque
names preserved, prelude untouched and readable. `--readable` /
`minify = false` in project.kira produce the pretty form for inspection.

## The rule

Any change that affects emitted C/JS (KiraCCodeGenerator.kt,
KiraJSCodeGenerator.kt, OutputMinifier.kt, CMagicTypeLowering.kt,
CIntrinsicsTable.kt, c_generator.c, c_bundle.h, js_generator.js,
kira/*.kira stdlib surface) runs `./gradlew test` before it lands:

- a test project that prints something else is a behaviour change: fix it,
  or, when the change is deliberate, update that `expected.txt` in the same
  commit, by hand, from a run you have checked;
- a prelude that differs between projects is a bug.
